Computer Science Seminar Series (HCI)

Do Students Ask for Help at the Right Time? Telemetry from Two Years of Intro=
ductory Programming Labs
Wednesday, January 21, 2026 | 12:30-1:30 PM | Torgersen 1100 (lunch provided,=
 RSVP below)
Speaker: Dr. K. Mendes, Department of Computer Science

Abstract: We logged editor activity, test runs and help requests in 14 CS1 la=
b sections over four semesters. Students who waited more than six minutes aft=
er a failing test before asking for help were much less likely to finish the =
lab, but students who asked within the first minute did not do better than th=
ose who waited two to four minutes. I will show what predicts a "productive w=
ait" and what TAs can see in real time.

